 "title": "Token bucket",
 "sources": [
  "Wikipedia, 'Token bucket' (secondary source, fetched 2026-11-17): a fixed-capacity bucket holds tokens; tokens are added at a fixed rate and tokens arriving when the bucket is full are discarded; a packet of n bytes needs n tokens, removed on send; a packet does not conform if there are insufficient tokens, and can be dropped, queued, or sent marked as non-conforming; the long-term rate is capped by the token rate while the bucket depth allows bursts. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Token_bucket",
  "Engineering consequence, not from the source: per-server buckets multiply a client's allowance by the number of servers; the ten-servers example is an illustration."
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "One client floods your API with requests, and suddenly everyone else gets slow responses.",
   "caps": "*ONE CLIENT FLOODS | EVERYONE *SLOWS DOWN"
  },
  {
   "text": "A token bucket stops that. Picture a bucket that holds a fixed number of tokens.",
   "caps": "*TOKEN BUCKET | A *FIXED NUMBER | OF TOKENS"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tokens drip in at a steady rate, and when the bucket is full, extra tokens are thrown away.",
   "caps": "TOKENS *DRIP IN | STEADY *RATE | FULL? *DISCARD"
  },
  {
   "text": "Every request takes a token. If the bucket has one, the request goes through.",
   "caps": "*EVERY REQUEST | TAKES A *TOKEN | *GOES THROUGH"
  },
  {
   "text": "If the bucket is empty, the request doesn't conform, so you reject it, or make it wait.",
   "caps": "BUCKET *EMPTY | *REJECT IT | OR *WAIT"
  },
  {
   "text": "That gives a nice property: the average rate is capped by the refill rate, but a full bucket still allows a short burst.",
   "caps": "AVERAGE *CAPPED | FULL BUCKET *ALLOWS BURSTS"
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the catch: if each server keeps its own bucket, a client hitting ten servers gets ten times the limit.",
   "caps": "BUT THERE IS A *CATCH | EACH SERVER *ITS OWN BUCKET | *10X THE LIMIT"
  },
  {
   "text": "So refill at a steady rate, size the bucket for the burst you'll allow, and share the counts across servers.",
   "caps": "*STEADY REFILL | SIZE FOR THE *BURST | *SHARE THE COUNTS"
  }
 ],
